---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import {places} from '../data/places';
const selected=places[0]!;
---
<Base title="Follow the current" description="Explore seven accurately located places through landscape, language and memory in Swat Valley." section="atlas">
<header class="atlas-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">A valley, in relation</span><h1>Follow the current.</h1></div><p>Keep a place in view.<br/>Change the way you see it.</p></header>
<div class="atlas-workspace" id="atlas" data-places={JSON.stringify(places)}><section class="atlas-geography" aria-label="Geographic exploration"><div id="map" aria-label="Interactive map of Swat Valley"></div><div id="coordinate-fallback"><svg viewBox="0 0 540 660" role="img" aria-labelledby="plot-title plot-desc"><title id="plot-title">Swat places plotted by longitude and latitude</title><desc id="plot-desc">Mahodand and Kalam lie north of Bahrain and Madyan. Mingora and Barikot are further south. Malam Jabba lies east of Mingora. This is a coordinate plot without terrain or river data.</desc><g fill="none" stroke="#668375" stroke-width=".5">{[72.2,72.4,72.6,72.8].map(lon=><path d={`M${(lon-72.05)/.8*460+40} 35v570`}/>)}{[34.7,35,35.3,35.6].map(lat=><path d={`M40 ${(35.82-lat)/1.22*570+35}h460`}/>)}</g><g fill="#d6dfb8" font-size="11" font-family="Arial">{[72.2,72.4,72.6,72.8].map(lon=><text x={(lon-72.05)/.8*460+40} y="635" text-anchor="middle">{lon}° E</text>)}{[34.7,35,35.3,35.6].map(lat=><text x="12" y={(35.82-lat)/1.22*570+35} transform={`rotate(-90 12 ${(35.82-lat)/1.22*570+35})`}>{lat}° N</text>)}</g>{places.map(p=><g><circle cx={(p.coordinates[0]-72.05)/.8*460+40} cy={(35.82-p.coordinates[1])/1.22*570+35} r="5" fill="#e9eac9"/><text x={(p.coordinates[0]-72.05)/.8*460+50} y={(35.82-p.coordinates[1])/1.22*570+31} fill="#eeeae1" font-family="Arial" font-size="12">{p.name}</text></g>)}</svg><p class="plot-note">Coordinate plot · No terrain or river course shown</p></div><div class="map-status" role="status"><span id="map-status">Loading geographic map…</span><button id="retry-map" hidden>Try map again</button></div><button class="map-reset" id="reset-map" hidden>Show whole valley ↗</button><span class="map-north" aria-hidden="true">N ↑</span><div class="map-credit">© <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> · <a href="https://openfreemap.org/">OpenFreeMap</a> · <a href="https://openmaptiles.org/">OpenMapTiles</a></div></section>
<section class="atlas-story" aria-label="Place and story lens"><div class="lens-tabs" aria-label="Story perspective">{['landscape','language','memory'].map((lens,i)=><button data-lens={lens} aria-pressed={i===0}>{lens}</button>)}</div><label class="eyebrow" for="place-select">Choose a place</label><select id="place-select">{places.map(p=><option value={p.id}>{p.name}</option>)}</select><div class="atlas-place" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><span id="atlas-region" class="eyebrow">{selected.region}</span><h2 id="atlas-name">{selected.name}</h2><img id="atlas-image" src={`/images/${selected.image}-960.webp`} alt="Mahodand Lake surrounded by meadow and mountains" width="960" height="640"/><p class="atlas-image-credit"><a id="atlas-credit" href={`/sources/#photo-${selected.image}`}>Photograph & license ↗</a></p><p id="atlas-text">{selected.lenses.landscape}</p><p id="atlas-coordinates" class="caption">{selected.coordinates[1]}° N / {selected.coordinates[0]}° E</p><a class="underlink" id="atlas-link" href={`/places/${selected.id}/`}>Read the Mahodand place note ↗</a></div><div class="atlas-step"><button id="previous-place" aria-label="Previous place">←</button><span id="place-progress">Upstream / Mahodand</span><button id="next-place" aria-label="Next place">→</button></div></section></div>
<section class="atlas-after"><div><span class="eyebrow">Reading this atlas</span><h2>One place.<br/>Three currents.</h2></div><div><p>The landscape lens follows geographical relationships. Language brings documented cultural connections into view. Memory connects archaeological and environmental records.</p><p>Markers show representative locations, not entrances, language boundaries or a travel itinerary. Malam Jabba sits east of the main river corridor. The map’s waterways come from geographic data; they are not hand-drawn decorative paths.</p><a class="underlink" href="/sources/#geography">Coordinates, data & attribution ↗</a></div></section><nav class="place-index" aria-label="Read all place notes"><span class="eyebrow">Continue on foot, through the reading</span><div class="place-index-list">{places.map(p=><a href={`/places/${p.id}/`}>{p.name} ↗</a>)}</div></nav>
<noscript><p class="section-space">The coordinate plot and place links work without JavaScript. Enable JavaScript to change lenses and explore the interactive map.</p></noscript><script src="../scripts/atlas.ts"></script>
</Base>
